#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Revert-the-fix proof (plan task P1.9): every guard must fail when the behavior it guards is broken.

For each mutation this copies the repository (scripts, schemas, tests, docs, skills, instructions) to a scratch folder, puts the
OLD behavior back with one exact text replacement, runs the one test file that guards it, and requires that file to FAIL. A
mutation whose anchor text no longer exists is reported as STALE (the proof must be updated), never silently skipped. The
unmodified copy must pass first, or the run is meaningless.

Usage: python plans/enhancements/evidence/mutation_proofs.py [--only ID ...]
Exit status: 0 when every mutation is caught, 1 otherwise.
"""
